                    %mi S
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{-S',(-)\}
              thus restricted is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derivation"} derivation
              of the Wick algebra product, it is sufficient to see that its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutators"} commutators
              with the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wightman+propagator"} Wightman propagator
              vanish in each argument:
            .maruku-equation
